        // For a continuous distribution, inverseCumulativeProbability(p) should return x such that
        // cumulativeProbability(x) == p for valid p in (0, 1). We build such p from the real API:
        // p = cumulativeProbability(k) for known integer k, so inverseCumulativeProbability(p)
        // must recover k (up to numerical tolerance). A patch that merely suppresses the throw
        // or returns a wrong value will violate this observable round-trip property.

