t;\n            }\n        }\n\n        /* Contract used below: a decimal string larger than Integer.MAX_VALUE but within long range\n           must be parsed by createNumber as a Long, matching createLong on the same canonical input. */\n        String longStr = \"2147483648\";\n        try {\n            Number parsedLong = NumberUtils.createNumber(longStr);\n            Long oracleLong = NumberUtils.createLong(longStr);\n            if (parsedLong == null || oracleLong == null\n                    || !parsedLong.getClass().equals(Long.class)\n                    || parsedLong.longValue() != oracleLong.longValue()) {\n                throw new RuntimeException(\n                        \"metamorphic violation: createNumber(long-range decimal) != createLong input=\"\n                                + longStr + \" lhs=\" + valueDesc(parsedLong) + \" rhs=\" + valueDesc(oracleLong));\n            }\n        } catch (RuntimeException t) {\n            if (isCleanRejection(t)) {\n                return;\n            }\n            if (isRootCause(t) || isMetamorphicFailure(t)) {\n                throw t;\n            }\n        }\n\n        /* Contract used below: valid scientific notation differs only by exponent-marker case.\n           Correct parsing must give equivalent results for e and E. If either side rejects, the\n           relation does not apply and is skipped. */\n        String mant = digitize(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 12)));\n        String exp = digitize(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 8)));\n        if (mant.length() == 0) {\n            mant = \"1\";\n        }\n        if (exp.length() == 0) {\n            exp = \"0\";\n        }\n        String sciLower = (data.consumeBoolean() ? \"-\" : \"\") + mant + \"e\" + exp;\n        String sciUpper = sciLower.replace('e', 'E');\n        try {\n            Number a = NumberUtils.createNumber(sciLower);\n            Number b = NumberUtils.createNumber(sciUpper);\n            if (a != null && b != null) {\n                if (!a.getClass().equals(b.getClass()) || a.doubleValue() != b.doubleValue()) {\n                    throw new RuntimeException(\n                            \"metamorphic violation: e/E equivalent scientific notation input=\"\n                                    + sciLower + \" lhs=\" + valueDesc(a) + \" rhs=\" + valueDesc(b));\n                }\n            }\n        } catch (RuntimeException t) {\n            if (isCleanRejection(t)) {\n                return;\n            }\n            if (isRootCause(t) || isMetamorphicFailure(t)) {\n                throw t;\n            }\n        }\n\n        /* Contract used below: D and d are equivalent requested types for a valid decimal literal. */\n        String whole = digitize(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 12)));\n        String frac = digitize(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 12)));\n        if (whole.length() == 0) {\n            whole = \"0\";\n        }\n        if (frac.length() == 0) {\n            frac = \"0\";\n        }\n        String decimal = (data.consumeBoolean() ? \"-\" : \"\") + whole + \".\" + frac;\n        try {\n            Number upper = NumberUtils.createNumber(decimal + \"D\");\n            Number lower = NumberUtils.createNumber(decimal + \"d\");\n            if (upper != null && lower != null) {\n                if (!upper.getClass().equals(lower.getClass()) || upper.doubleValue() != lower.doubleValue()) {\n                    throw new RuntimeException(\n                            \"metamorphic violation: D/d suffix equivalence input=\"\n                                    + decimal + \" lhs=\" + valueDesc(upper) + \" rhs=\" + valueDesc(lower));\n                }\n            }\n        } catch (RuntimeException t) {\n            if (isCleanRejection(t)) {\n                return;\n            }\n            if (isRootCause(t) || isMetamorphicFailure(t)) {\n                throw t;\n            }\n        }\n    }",
        "private static void exercise(String s) {\n        try {\n            NumberUtils.createNumber(s);\n        } catch (RuntimeException t) {\n            if (isCleanRejection(t)) {\n                return;\n            }\n            if (isRootCause(t)) {\n                throw t;\n            }\n        }\n    }",
        "private static void exerciseKnownLiteral(String s) {\n        try {\n            NumberUtils.createNumber(s);\n        } catch (RuntimeException t) {\n            if (isValidationRejection(t)) {\n                return;\n            }\n            if (isRootCause(t)) {\n                throw new RuntimeException(\"metamorphic violation: documented/seed literal should be handled without internal substring failure input=\" + quote(s), t);\n            }\n        }\n    }",
        "private static void checkValidPlainDecimal(String s) {\n        /*\n         * Contract used for this check:\n         * For a valid decimal string with a decimal point and no exponent/suffix,\n         * createNumber goes down the float/double/bigdecimal path. For small,\n         * finite, non-underflowing decimals such as the ones we construct here,\n         * the implementation first creates a Float and returns it.\n         * Therefore, for these valid-by-construction inputs, createNumber(s)\n         * must agree with createFloat(s), and a patch that merely suppresses\n         * the old crash or skips the intended parsing branch would violate this.\n         */\n        Float oracle;\n        try {\n            oracle = NumberUtils.createFloat(s);\n        } catch (RuntimeException t) {\n            return;\n        }\n\n        try {\n            Number parsed = NumberUtils.createNumber(s);\n            if (!(parsed instanceof Float) || !oracle.equals(parsed)) {\n                throw new RuntimeException(\n                        \"metamorphic violation: createNumber(valid plain decimal) != createFloat input=\"\n                                + quote(s) + \" oracle=\" + oracle + \" parsed=\"\n                                + String.valueOf(parsed) + \" parsedClass=\"\n                                + (parsed == null ? \"null\" : parsed.getClass().getName()));\n            }\n        } catch (RuntimeException t) {\n            if (isValidationRejection(t)) {\n                return;\n            }\n            if (isRootCause(t)) {\n                throw new RuntimeException(\n                        \"metamorphic violation: valid plain decimal should parse like createFloat input=\"\n                                + quote(s) + \" oracle=\" + oracle, t);\n            }\n        }\n    }",
        "private static void checkCanonicalInteger(String s) {\n        /*\n         * Contract used for this check:\n         * For a canonical base-10 integer string with no suffix, createNumber\n         * tries createInteger first, then wider integral types only on overflow.\n         * Thus when we build s from Integer.toString(int)-style digits in range,\n         * createNumber(s) must agree with createInteger(s).\n         */\n        try {\n            Integer oracle = NumberUtils.createInteger(s);\n            Number parsed = NumberUtils.createNumber(s);\n            if (oracle != null && parsed != null) {\n                if (!(parsed instanceof Integer) || parsed.intValue() != oracle.intValue()) {\n                    throw new RuntimeException(\n                            \"metamorphic violation: createNumber(canonical int) != createInteger input=\"\n                                    + quote(s) + \" oracle=\" + oracle + \" parsed=\"\n                                    + String.valueOf(parsed) + \" parsedClass=\"\n                                    + parsed.getClass().getName());\n                }\n            }\n        } catch (RuntimeException t) {\n            if (isValidationRejection(t)) {\n                return;\n            }\n            if (isRootCause(t)) {\n                throw new RuntimeException(\n                        \"metamorphic violation: canonical integer should not hit internal substring failure input=\"\n                                + quote(s), t);\n            }\n        }\n    }",
        "public static void fuzzerTestOneInput(com.code_intelligence.jazzer.api.FuzzedDataProvider data) {\n        callTarget(\"1eE\");\n\n        String left = nonEmptyDigits(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 8)));\n        String middle = digitsOnly(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 8)));\n        String right = digitsOnly(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 8)));\n\n        callTarget(left + \"e\" + middle + \"E\" + right);\n        callTarget(left + \"E\" + middle + \"e\" + right);\n\n        String prefix = data.consumeBoolean() ? \"-\" : \"\";\n        callTarget(prefix + left + \"e\" + middle + \"E\");\n        callTarget(prefix + left + \"E\" + middle + \"e\");\n\n        int known = data.consumeInt();\n        String intStr = Integer.toString(known);\n\n        /*\n         * Contract: for a canonical base-10 integer string, createNumber first tries\n         * createInteger and should return the same Integer result when it fits.\n         * A patch that merely avoids the buggy throw by skipping/altering the normal\n         * parsing path would violate this observable relation.\n         */\n        Number a = NumberUtils.createNumber(intStr);\n        Integer b = NumberUtils.createInteger(intStr);\n        if (a == null || b == null || !(a instanceof Integer) || a.intValue() != b.intValue()) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(\n                    \"metamorphic violation: createNumber(canonical int) != createInteger input=\"\n                            + quote(intStr) + \" lhs=\" + String.valueOf(a) + \" rhs=\" + String.valueOf(b));\n        }\n\n        String frac = nonEmptyDigits(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 8)));\n        String dec = prefix + left + \".\" + frac;\n        try {\n            Number upper = NumberUtils.createNumber(dec + \"D\");\n            Number lower = NumberUtils.createNumber(dec + \"d\");\n            if (upper != null && lower != null && upper.doubleValue() != lower.doubleValue()) {\n                throw new RuntimeException(\n                        \"metamorphic violation: D/d suffix equivalence input=\"\n                                + quote(dec) + \" lhs=\" + String.valueOf(upper) + \" rhs=\" + String.valueOf(lower));\n            }\n        } catch (RuntimeException t) {\n            if (!isValidationRejection(t)) {\n                throw t;\n            }\n        }\n    }",
        "public static void fuzzerTestOneInput(com.code_intelligence.jazzer.api.FuzzedDataProvider data) {\n        callTarget(\"1eE\");\n\n        String left = nonEmptyDigits(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 8)));\n        String middle = digitsOnly(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 8)));\n        String right = digitsOnly(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 8)));\n\n        callTarget(left + \"e\" + middle + \"E\" + right);\n        callTarget(left + \"E\" + middle + \"e\" + right);\n\n        String prefix = data.consumeBoolean() ? \"-\" : \"\";\n        callTarget(prefix + left + \"e\" + middle + \"E\");\n        callTarget(prefix + left + \"E\" + middle + \"e\");\n\n        int known = data.consumeInt();\n        String intStr = Integer.toString(known);\n\n        /*\n         * Contract: for a canonical base-10 integer string, createNumber first tries\n         * createInteger and should return the same Integer result when it fits.\n         * A patch that merely avoids the buggy throw by skipping/altering the normal\n         * parsing path would violate this observable relation.\n         */\n        Number a = NumberUtils.createNumber(intStr);\n        Integer b = NumberUtils.createInteger(intStr);\n        if (a == null || b == null || !(a instanceof Integer) || a.intValue() != b.intValue()) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(\n                    \"metamorphic violation: createNumber(canonical int) != createInteger input=\"\n                            + quote(intStr) + \" lhs=\" + String.valueOf(a) + \" rhs=\" + String.valueOf(b));\n        }\n\n        String frac = nonEmptyDigits(data.consumeAsciiString(data.consumeInt(0, 8)));\n        String dec = prefix + left + \".\" + frac;\n        try {\n            Number upper = NumberUtils.createNumber(dec + \"D\");\n            Number lower = NumberUtils.createNumber(dec + \"d\");\n            if (upper != null && lower != null && upper.doubleValue() != lower.doubleValue()) {\n                throw new RuntimeException(\n                        \"metamorphic violation: D/d suffix equivalence input=\"\n                                + quote(dec) + \" lhs=\" + String.valueOf(upper) + \" rhs=\" + String.valueOf(lower));\n            }\n        } catch (RuntimeException t) {\n            if (!isValidationRejection(t)) {\n                throw t;\n            }\n        }\n    }",
        "private static void callTarget(String s) {\n        try {\n            NumberUtils.createNumber(s);\n        } catch (RuntimeException t) {\n            if (isValidationRejection(t)) {\n                return;\n            }\n            if (isRootCause(t)) {\n                throw t;\n            }\n            throw t;\n        }\n    }",
        "public void testCreateNumber() {\n        // a lot of things can go wrong\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 1 failed\", new Float(\"1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1234.5\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 2 failed\", new Integer(\"12345\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"12345\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 3 failed\", new Double(\"1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1234.5D\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 3 failed\", new Double(\"1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1234.5d\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 4 failed\", new Float(\"1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1234.5F\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 4 failed\", new Float(\"1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1234.5f\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 5 failed\", new Long(Integer.MAX_VALUE + 1L), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"\"\n            + (Integer.MAX_VALUE + 1L)));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 6 failed\", new Long(12345), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"12345L\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 6 failed\", new Long(12345), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"12345l\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 7 failed\", new Float(\"-1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"-1234.5\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 8 failed\", new Integer(\"-12345\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"-12345\"));\n        assertTrue(\"createNumber(String) 9 failed\", 0xFADE == NumberUtils.createNumber(\"0xFADE\").intValue());\n        assertTrue(\"createNumber(String) 10 failed\", -0xFADE == NumberUtils.createNumber(\"-0xFADE\").intValue());\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 11 failed\", new Double(\"1.1E200\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1.1E200\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 12 failed\", new Float(\"1.1E20\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1.1E20\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 13 failed\", new Double(\"-1.1E200\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"-1.1E200\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 14 failed\", new Double(\"1.1E-200\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1.1E-200\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(null) failed\", null, NumberUtils.createNumber(null));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) failed\", new BigInteger(\"12345678901234567890\"), NumberUtils\n                .createNumber(\"12345678901234567890L\"));\n\n        // jdk 1.2 doesn't support this. unsure about jdk 1.2.2\n        if (SystemUtils.isJavaVersionAtLeast(1.3f)) {\n            assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 15 failed\", new BigDecimal(\"1.1E-700\"), NumberUtils\n                    .createNumber(\"1.1E-700F\"));\n        }\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 16 failed\", new Long(\"10\" + Integer.MAX_VALUE), NumberUtils\n                .createNumber(\"10\" + Integer.MAX_VALUE + \"L\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 17 failed\", new Long(\"10\" + Integer.MAX_VALUE), NumberUtils\n                .createNumber(\"10\" + Integer.MAX_VALUE));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 18 failed\", new BigInteger(\"10\" + Long.MAX_VALUE), NumberUtils\n                .createNumber(\"10\" + Long.MAX_VALUE));\n\n        // LANG-521\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) LANG-521 failed\", new Float(\"2.\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"2.\"));\n\n        // LANG-638\n        assertFalse(\"createNumber(String) succeeded\", checkCreateNumber(\"1eE\"));\n    }",
        "public void testCreateNumber() {\n        // a lot of things can go wrong\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 1 failed\", new Float(\"1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1234.5\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 2 failed\", new Integer(\"12345\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"12345\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 3 failed\", new Double(\"1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1234.5D\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 3 failed\", new Double(\"1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1234.5d\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 4 failed\", new Float(\"1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1234.5F\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 4 failed\", new Float(\"1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1234.5f\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 5 failed\", new Long(Integer.MAX_VALUE + 1L), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"\"\n            + (Integer.MAX_VALUE + 1L)));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 6 failed\", new Long(12345), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"12345L\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 6 failed\", new Long(12345), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"12345l\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 7 failed\", new Float(\"-1234.5\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"-1234.5\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 8 failed\", new Integer(\"-12345\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"-12345\"));\n        assertTrue(\"createNumber(String) 9 failed\", 0xFADE == NumberUtils.createNumber(\"0xFADE\").intValue());\n        assertTrue(\"createNumber(String) 10 failed\", -0xFADE == NumberUtils.createNumber(\"-0xFADE\").intValue());\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 11 failed\", new Double(\"1.1E200\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1.1E200\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 12 failed\", new Float(\"1.1E20\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1.1E20\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 13 failed\", new Double(\"-1.1E200\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"-1.1E200\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 14 failed\", new Double(\"1.1E-200\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"1.1E-200\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(null) failed\", null, NumberUtils.createNumber(null));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) failed\", new BigInteger(\"12345678901234567890\"), NumberUtils\n                .createNumber(\"12345678901234567890L\"));\n\n        // jdk 1.2 doesn't support this. unsure about jdk 1.2.2\n        if (SystemUtils.isJavaVersionAtLeast(1.3f)) {\n            assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 15 failed\", new BigDecimal(\"1.1E-700\"), NumberUtils\n                    .createNumber(\"1.1E-700F\"));\n        }\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 16 failed\", new Long(\"10\" + Integer.MAX_VALUE), NumberUtils\n                .createNumber(\"10\" + Integer.MAX_VALUE + \"L\"));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 17 failed\", new Long(\"10\" + Integer.MAX_VALUE), NumberUtils\n                .createNumber(\"10\" + Integer.MAX_VALUE));\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) 18 failed\", new BigInteger(\"10\" + Long.MAX_VALUE), NumberUtils\n                .createNumber(\"10\" + Long.MAX_VALUE));\n\n        // LANG-521\n        assertEquals(\"createNumber(String) LANG-521 failed\", new Float(\"2.\"), NumberUtils.createNumber(\"2.\"));\n\n        // LANG-638\n        assertFalse(\"createNumber(String) succeeded\", checkCreateNumber(\"1eE\"));\n    }",
